<title>TUNISIA: Tunisia grants licence to Maghreb rating agency.</title>
<headline>Tunisia grants licence to Maghreb rating agency.</headline>
<dateline>TUNIS 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tunisia has granted a licence to Maghreb Rating, the first company set up in the North African country to rate the region's companies, officials said on Thursday.</p>
<p>They said that Maghreb Rating was a subsidiary of Inter Arab Rating Company (IARC), a rating firm sponsored by the Arab Monetary Fund (AMF).</p>
<p>The agency will cover Tunisia, Morocco, Algeria, Libya and Mauritania.</p>
<p>Hazim al-Dalli was named chairman of Maghreb Rating.</p>
<p>Tunis newsroom, 2161-787538</p>
</text>
